    "body": "## Mandatory audit of the uploaded A1–A104 knowledge package (do not restart from zero)\n\nRead `CONSTITUTION_V2.md`, `docs/S92_GRAPHICS_VERIFICATION.md`, and `docs/knowledge-transfer/A1_A104_PRIMARY_CODER_AUDIT.md` first. Then audit the original A1–A104 claims against the current source, commit history, and existing runtime artifacts.\n\nFor **each claim**, add a line-by-line verdict: **ACCEPTED / REJECTED / PARTIAL / NEEDS REPRODUCTION**, with the exact source file + function/line, commit or test/evidence reference, reason, and next action. Do not infer a fix from a screenshot label or a successful build. Do not rerun everything if existing fresh evidence already proves it; do not accept a claim without evidence.\n\n**First resolve a transfer-integrity gap:** the attached ZIP contains only a partial A1–A104 narrative (A1–A50 grouped, then selected IDs, and A104); many IDs are not described there. Reconcile it with the repository audit document before calling the package “complete.” The ZIP's mosaic shows six nonblank game screenshots and a white dooz frame, but the images alone do **not** prove three-run SHA identity, interaction/state change, binary identity, or the claimed root causes. Inspect the original hash/run logs if present.\n\nDo not start A105+ or broad implementation work until this audit is complete. Finish with counts per verdict and the **fewest targeted reproductions needed** to settle unresolved claims. Preserve historical statuses; no unsupported promotions.",
